# Capsule delivery volume (WIC kickstart).
#
# GPT with a single 64 MiB FAT32 EFI System Partition carrying
# \EFI\UpdateCapsule\RPi5Firmware.cap -- deliberately the same shape as the
# volume nanokvm-app's pkg/firmware builds at runtime with go-diskfs and
# presents on the mass-storage gadget's lun.0 (GPT + FAT32 ESP + the spec's
# capsule drop-box directory, UEFI 2.10 8.5.5), so whatever scans one format
# scans both. FAT32 is forced with --mkfs-extraopts: at 64 MiB mkdosfs would
# otherwise pick FAT16, and the runtime volume is explicitly FAT32.
#
# --fixed-size 64M is load-bearing, not padding: FAT32 needs >= 65525
# clusters to BE FAT32 -- on a content-sized (~18 MiB) partition a forced
# "-F 32" produces an out-of-spec volume that FAT drivers, EDK2's included,
# may classify as FAT16 from the cluster count and then fail to read. The
# empty space costs nothing after wic.xz compression.
#
# Populated from the capsule-staging tree the recipe assembles and passes as
# the default ROOTFS_DIR (WIC_CREATE_EXTRA_ARGS), same mechanism as
# rpi5-uefi.wks.
#
# Keep the part directive on one line: wic's kickstart parser shlex-splits
# each line and does not join backslash continuations.

bootloader --ptable gpt

part /boot --source rootfs --rootfs-dir=ROOTFS_DIR --fstype=vfat --label CAPSULE --part-type C12A7328-F81F-11D2-BA4B-00A0C93EC93B --align 1024 --fixed-size 64M --mkfs-extraopts "-F 32"
